cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GraphGWAS, please cite both the software and the accompanying paper."
title: "GraphGWAS: relational fine-mapping of causal GWAS variants on a multi-omics knowledge graph"
abstract: >
  GraphGWAS is a graph-native fine-mapping platform. Annotations register
  as typed edges on a labelled-property graph database; fine-mapping is
  computed by message passing (HBP) or annotation-adaptive Bayesian
  scoring (GAFM) over the variant--gene--pathway factor graph rather
  than as regression with flattened scalar weights. This Zenodo deposit
  contains the source-code release, pre-built graph-database dumps,
  benchmark JSON outputs, multi-omics graph caches, IRRI 3kRG
  summary statistics, cross-species lead lists, Pan-UK Biobank
  per-locus fine-mapping outputs, simulation seeds, and figure source
  data accompanying the manuscript.
type: software
